  "id": "20",
  "name": "Manufacture of chemicals and chemical products",
  "section": "C",
  "summary": "Chemical companies report AI in R&D (materials informatics, AI-driven formulation, inverse design, self-driving labs, in silico toxicology), in plant operations (advanced process control, autonomous plants, soft sensors, predictive maintenance) and in pricing and supply chain. AI is also a major demand driver: semiconductor materials, photoresists, specialty gases, low-dielectric resins, thermal interface materials and immersion cooling fluids for AI servers and data centres, with electricity cost and export controls as related risks. Sub-sectors add their own vocabulary: digital farming for agrochemicals and fertilisers, colour matching for coatings, beauty tech and AI fragrance creation for consumer chemicals, digital blasting for explosives.",
